# NOTE: Render does not read this file — it is not Netlify.
# The authoritative redirect rules live in render.yaml under
# services[0].routes. This file is kept only because the local
# test server (server/server.js) reads it, so the dev server and
# production stay in agreement. Update BOTH if you add a rule.
#
# Destinations updated 2026-09-15 to the routed URL scheme. Since the routing
# migration the writers' pages live under /writers/, so the previous targets
# (/writing/, /writing-opportunities/) do not exist in the published artifact
# and every rule below was 301ing to a 404. Verified against public/ at
# 563f734: public/writing/ and public/writing-opportunities/ are absent, while
# public/writers/writing/ and public/writers/writing-opportunities/ are present
# and index,follow. scripts/validate-http.js now asserts that each redirect
# destination resolves, so this cannot silently regress again.
#
# Writing-first BRYME launch. Legacy multi-niche hubs (jobs, opportunities,
# make-money) were retired and live on the legacy-multiniche branch.
# Keep 301s so old links land on the closest living writing-first surface.
# 2026-09-16: the three retired hub roots (/opportunities, /jobs, /make-money)
# are no longer rules — they are file-level stubs generated into public/ by
# scripts/purge-stale-publish.py (noindex + meta-refresh to /writers/writing/).
# Render never read this file, and the live service's dashboard-era rules were
# never synced from render.yaml, so the stubs are the enforcement that actually
# ships; a published file also wins over any rule, so keeping both was moot.
# The nested legacy path below has no stub twin and stays a rule.
/make-money/writing-opportunities/  /writers/writing-opportunities/  301
